{#
  What the hub's house-status poll reads, built from the inventory so no hostname
  is hardcoded. An object with two lists:

  "targets": every host's own status file, by its inventory key, plus the
  nightstand frame's status file that the hub serves on the bedroom machine. The
  bedroom machine is found by its stable host_id (unchanged by any hostname
  rename), so this follows a rename of the key automatically. The frame is
  labelled "nightstand-frame", not "nightstand", so it does not collide with the
  bedroom machine once that machine's key is renamed to nightstand. The
  "/nightstand/" path is the nginx alias the web role serves and is unrelated to
  the hostname.

  "frames": every frame host (one whose roles include nightstand_bootstrap), as
  {"id", "base"}. The hub republishes each frame's art history and mirror from
  base under /frames/<id>/. base is the "/nightstand/" alias the frame serves its
  own files at.

  snaphouse.housestatus reads this file and writes house-status.json plus the
  per-frame mirrors. It still accepts the old bare-list shape, so a hub updated
  before this template is re-rendered keeps working. Hostnames are mDNS .local
  names from the cross-repo status contract; nothing identifying.
#}
{% set targets = [] %}
{% for name in snaphouse_hosts.keys() %}
{% set _ = targets.append({'name': name, 'url': 'http://' ~ name ~ '.local/status.json'}) %}
{% endfor %}
{% set bedroom_host = (snaphouse_hosts | dict2items | selectattr('value.host_id', 'equalto', 'bedroom') | map(attribute='key') | first) %}
{% set _ = targets.append({'name': 'nightstand-frame', 'url': 'http://' ~ bedroom_host ~ '.local/nightstand/status.json'}) %}
{% set frames = [] %}
{% for name, spec in snaphouse_hosts.items() %}
{% if 'nightstand_bootstrap' in spec.roles %}
{% set _ = frames.append({'id': name, 'base': 'http://' ~ name ~ '.local/nightstand/'}) %}
{% endif %}
{% endfor %}
{{ {'targets': targets, 'frames': frames} | to_nice_json }}
